// REJECTED — a call through an arrow *value* supplying the wrong number of
// arguments (roadmap item 75(a)). The arrow-value twin of t10_call_arity: an
// arrow's arity is purely syntactic and never in doubt, so it is checked even
// when nothing about the parameter's type is known. revl has no default,
// optional, or variadic parameters, so arity is exact.
//
// Before item 75(a) an arrow with any un-annotated parameter had no type at
// all, which threw the arity away with it, and `f(1, 2)` compiled. rust reports
// E0061 ("this function takes 1 argument but 2 arguments were supplied") and
// javac "method cannot be applied to given types"; python raises only at run
// time.
//
// expected error:
//   `f` is a `(Any) -> Str` and takes 1 argument(s), 2 given

fn demo() -> Str {
  let f = (x) => "s"
  return f(1, 2)
}
